BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:hm-foundation-global-change-award-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261025T090229Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261002
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261003
SUMMARY:Deadline: H&M Foundation: Global Change Award 2027 (via The Mills F
 abrica nomination window)
DESCRIPTION:The H&M Foundation backs ten changemakers each year with a EUR 
 200\,000 grant to accelerate early-stage innovation toward a net-zero text
 ile industry\; since 2015 the award has distributed a combined EUR 10 mill
 ion to 56 innovations. The foundation's FAQ states applicants can be an in
 dividual\, a small team or an organisation\, with no registered-company re
 quirement\, and ideas can still be at research\, lab or concept stage. Nei
 ther the Foundation\, its partners nor H&M Group take any equity or IP rig
 hts\, so this is a genuine grant\, not an investment vehicle. CATEGORIES: 
 sustainable materials\, responsible production\, mindful consumption\, and
  wildcards. WHAT YOU GET: EUR 200\,000 plus a yearlong Changemaker Program
 me with industry knowledge\, tools and connections. HOW TO APPLY: the 2027
  cycle is nomination-based\; The Mills Fabrica is an official nominator ac
 cepting open proposals from 1 September to 2 October 2026 via its website.
  DEADLINE: 2 October 2026 for the Mills Fabrica proposal window.\n\nOrgani
 sation: H&M Foundation (proposals via official nominator The Mills Fabrica
 )\nLocation: Worldwide. Open to early-stage textile and fashion innovators
 \; individuals\, small teams and organisations\, no registered-company req
 uirement.\nAward: EUR 200\,000 grant per winner\, ten winners annually\, p
 lus a yearlong Changemaker Programme. No equity or IP is taken. Participat
 ion is free of charge.\nDuration: Yearlong Changemaker Programme accompani
 es the grant.\n\nMore: https://hmfoundation.com/gca/?utm_source=artificial
 nouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://hmfoundation.com/gca/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm
 _medium=referral
LOCATION:Worldwide. Open to early-stage textile and fashion innovators\; in
 dividuals\, small teams and organisations\, no registered-company requirem
 ent.
