UID:stage-ix-round-2-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261025T090229Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261016
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261017
SUMMARY:Deadline: Stage IX Round 2: Immersive Art-Tech Research Residency (
 Fort Penningsveer)
DESCRIPTION:Stage IX is a practice-based research residency for immersive a
 rt\, technology and science\, run by Ruimtetijd at Fort Penningsveer with 
 NXT Museum\, 4DSOUND\, the Amsterdam University of the Arts (AHK)\, CWI an
 d POPKRAFT\, and funded through CIIIC/Stimuleringsfonds. Round 2 opened 15
  September 2026 and offers four positions: two on the Emerging track (2 to
  4 years of professional practice) and two on the Established track (5 or 
 more years). Residents pursue eight months of supported research from Janu
 ary 2027 (extendable to ten) in practice areas including spatial sound\, V
 R/XR/AR\, gamified and interactive media\, kinetic and light-based install
 ation\, scenography and immersive theatre\, with access to the partners' s
 tudios\, technology and mentorship. Open to Netherlands-based artists only
 . An online info session ran 23 September 2026\; details at stage-ix.com. 
 TO APPLY: submit via the Tally application form. DEADLINE: 16 October 2026
 .\n\nOrganisation: Stage IX (Ruimtetijd\, NXT Museum\, 4DSOUND\, AHK\, CWI
 \, POPKRAFT)\nLocation: Fort Penningsveer\, near Haarlem\, Netherlands. Ne
 therlands-based artists only.\nAward: Emerging track (2 to 4 years of prac
 tice\, 2 positions): EUR 18\,000 artist fee plus EUR 5\,000 R&D budget. Es
 tablished track (5+ years\, 2 positions): EUR 26\,000 artist fee plus EUR 
 15\,000 R&D budget. No application fee.\nDuration: 8 months of supported r
 esearch from January 2027\, extendable to 10 months.\n\nMore: https://tall
 y.so/r/PdxbrQ?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://tally.so/r/PdxbrQ?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_med
 ium=referral
LOCATION:Fort Penningsveer\, near Haarlem\, Netherlands. Netherlands-based 
 artists only.
