UID:acc-next-emerging-asian-artists-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261025T090229Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261025
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261026
SUMMARY:Deadline: 2027 ACC NEXT Emerging Asian Artists International Open C
 all (Gwangju)
DESCRIPTION:The National Asian Culture Center (ACC) in Gwangju seeks bold\,
  experimental work by emerging artists from Asia at the intersection of ar
 t and technology for its 2027 ACC NEXT exhibition. The theme is Prototype\
 ; works must not have been presented in another exhibition\, or must be re
 -created works. MEDIUMS: interactive installations (physical computing\, s
 ensor-based)\, generative video and image (code- and algorithm-based)\, ki
 netic and robotic art\, immersive and extended reality (XR)\, and related 
 work. SUPPORT: an artist fee of KRW 3\,000\,000 per work\, an installation
  and materials budget of up to KRW 2\,000\,000 per work\, one round-trip i
 nternational airfare for overseas residents (or domestic transportation)\,
  and tentative accommodation at Asia Plex Studio\; for teams\, support goe
 s to the team leader only. One artist or team is also selected for the 202
 7 ACC CREATORS Residency via an artist pitch review. ELIGIBILITY: national
 s of an Asian country born on or after 1 January 1987 (artists born or rai
 sed in Asia whose practice deeply engages with Asian identities may be con
 sidered regardless of nationality)\; at least one solo exhibition\, one ex
 hibition at a national or public art museum\, or three group exhibitions (
 art fairs and degree shows do not count)\; non-Korean nationals must be el
 igible for a Korean visa\; must be able to attend the installation\, openi
 ng and artist pitch. HOW TO APPLY: create an account on the ACC website an
 d submit online\, 1 to 25 October 2026\, as PDFs (max 50 MB each): applica
 tion form (ACC template)\, technical rider (ACC template)\, and a portfoli
 o including CV as a single file. Results announced 30 November 2026. DEADL
 INE: 25 October 2026 at 11:59 PM KST.\n\nOrganisation: National Asian Cult
 ure Center (ACC)\nLocation: National Asian Culture Center\, Gwangju\, Sout
 h Korea. Open to nationals of Asian countries born on or after 1 January 1
 987\; artists born or raised in Asia whose practice deeply engages with As
 ian identities may also be considered regardless of nationality.\nAward: A
 rtist fee of KRW 3\,000\,000 per work\, an installation and materials budg
 et of up to KRW 2\,000\,000 per work\, one round-trip international airfar
 e (or domestic transportation)\, and tentative accommodation at Asia Plex 
 Studio. One artist or team is additionally selected for the 2027 ACC CREAT
 ORS Residency through an artist pitch review. For teams\, fees\, travel an
 d accommodation go to the team leader only.\nDuration: Exhibition of selec
 ted works at ACC in 2027\; selected artists must attend the installation\,
  opening and artist pitch\n\nMore: https://www.acc.go.kr/en/board/board.do
 ?PID=1001&boardID=NOTICE&action=Read&idx=2866&utm_source=artificialnouveau
 grantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.acc.go.kr/en/board/board.do?PID=1001&boardID=NOTICE&action=
 Read&idx=2866&utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:National Asian Culture Center\, Gwangju\, South Korea. Open to nat
 ionals of Asian countries born on or after 1 January 1987\; artists born o
 r raised in Asia whose practice deeply engages with Asian identities may a
 lso be considered regardless of nationality.
END:VEVENT
