UID:data-through-design-2027-open-call@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261025T090229Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261115
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261116
SUMMARY:Deadline: Data Through Design 2027 Open Call: 10th Anniversary Exhi
 bition (New York City)
DESCRIPTION:Data Through Design\, the annual exhibition of artworks that cr
 eatively analyze\, interpret and interrogate data from New York City's Ope
 n Data portal\, opens its 10th anniversary call\, held in conjunction with
  NYC Open Data Week. THEME: reflections\, reverberations and the arc of da
 ta over time\; the evidence of time (footprints\, traces\, scars\, markers
  of change)\, temporal mirrors and kaleidoscopes\, messages from the past 
 and future\, fractals of time and visuals of scale. Artists may also respo
 nd to a previous DxD theme in light of time\, and alumni artists are parti
 cularly encouraged to apply\, including by revisiting past projects. FORMA
 TS: digital\, analog\, physical\, performance\, sound works\, walks\, inst
 allations\, creative coding\, participatory mapping\, drawings and more\; 
 the organizers highlight participatory data collection\, radical and cogni
 tive mapping\, and data experienced through time\, sound and the senses. R
 EQUIREMENT: projects must reference or use at least one NYC Open Data data
 set\; other data\, including novel and experimental collection systems\, i
 s welcome alongside it. WHAT YOU GET: USD 900 stipend\, half before and ha
 lf after the exhibition\, plus inclusion in the multi-media group show in 
 New York City\, tentatively 26 March to 11 April 2027. Work must be instal
 lation-ready by 19 March 2027 and delivered to the venue 22 to 24 March. E
 LIGIBILITY: open to artists\, civic technologists\, data enthusiasts\, cit
 y dwellers and creative practitioners\; applicants must be approved to wor
 k in the US to be paid the stipend. The submission process has been revamp
 ed for this edition\, with a new rubric and submission materials to review
 . APPLICATION: free\, via the submission form on the DxD website. DEADLINE
 : 15 November 2026 at 23:59 EST.\n\nOrganisation: Data Through Design (DxD
 )\nLocation: New York City\, USA. Open call\; applicants must be approved 
 to work in the US to be paid the stipend.\nAward: USD 900 stipend per sele
 cted project\, paid half in the weeks leading up to the exhibition and hal
 f after. No application fee.\nDuration: Exhibition tentatively 26 March to
  11 April 2027\; work installation-ready by 19 March and delivered to the 
 venue 22 to 24 March 2027.\n\nMore: https://datathroughdesign.com/open-cal
 l-2027?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://datathroughdesign.com/open-call-2027?utm_source=artificialnouve
 augrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:New York City\, USA. Open call\; applicants must be approved to wo
 rk in the US to be paid the stipend.
END:VEVENT
