SUMMARY:Deadline: Internet Society Fellowship Program 2027
DESCRIPTION:The Internet Society Fellowship supports people advancing Inter
 net connectivity\, policy or security in their communities. Fellows design
  and implement a practical project with deliverables such as policy briefs
 \, research reports\, training programs\, community engagement initiatives
 \, workshops or technical resources\, supported by a stipend of up to USD 
 5\,000\, a dedicated mentor\, weekly virtual training sessions and funded 
 travel to a global or regional Internet event. IMPORTANT PREREQUISITE: app
 licants must first complete the Pre-Fellowship Training modules\; enrollme
 nt for the training runs 23 September to 22 November 2026\, and eligible p
 articipants receive the Fellowship application link by email within 24 hou
 rs of completing it. ELIGIBILITY: open worldwide\; requires a high level o
 f English reading\, speaking and writing\, continuous Internet access thro
 ughout the program\, a valid passport (six months beyond anticipated trave
 l)\, at least four hours per week over 10 months\, and not currently parti
 cipating in a 2026 Internet Society fellowship. TIMELINE: applications rev
 iewed on a rolling basis and close 18 December 2026\; notifications 19 Feb
 ruary 2027\; program kick-off 22 February 2027\; project execution 1 June 
 to 30 November 2027\; graduation early December 2027.\n\nOrganisation: Int
 ernet Society\nLocation: Remote\, worldwide\, with funded travel to one gl
 obal or regional Internet event. Requires continuous Internet access\, str
 ong English\, and a passport valid at least six months beyond the anticipa
 ted travel.\nAward: Project stipend of up to USD 5\,000 (upon submission a
 nd approval of the project budget)\, plus travel support to attend a globa
 l or regional Internet event and a dedicated mentor aligned with the proje
 ct area. No application fee.\nDuration: 10 months (kick-off 22 February 20
 27\, graduation early December 2027)\, including a six-month mentored proj
 ect execution period from 1 June to 30 November 2027. Minimum commitment o
 f four hours per week.\n\nMore: https://www.internetsociety.org/fellowship
 /?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.internetsociety.org/fellowship/?utm_source=artificialnouvea
 ugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Remote\, worldwide\, with funded travel to one global or regional 
 Internet event. Requires continuous Internet access\, strong English\, and
  a passport valid at least six months beyond the anticipated travel.
END:VEVENT
