SUMMARY:Deadline: NLnet Foundation: Open Call November 2026 (Restack\, Code
 Supply and general fund)
DESCRIPTION:NLnet's current open call funds open-source technical developme
 nt: software and hardware released under free licenses. ROUTES: the Restac
 k fund (open internet stack)\, the CodeSupply fund\, and the general open 
 call for everything else\; accessibility and assistive-tech FOSS (screen r
 eaders\, a11y tooling\, accessible interfaces) was repeatedly funded under
  the predecessor NGI Zero programme and fits via the general route\, thoug
 h Restack's own scope text does not name accessibility\, so confirm scope 
 with NLnet before applying. NLnet also provides grantee support services i
 ncluding accessibility audits. ELIGIBILITY: individuals\, informal collect
 ives\, nonprofits\, SMEs and universities from any country\; no disability
  identification required. NOTE: proposals and projects generated with AI/L
 LMs are ineligible. APPLICATION: short online form at nlnet.nl/propose\; d
 ecisions within weeks\; calls recur roughly every two months\, so a missed
  deadline rolls to the next cycle. DEADLINE: 3 November 2026\, 12:00 CET (
 noon).\n\nOrganisation: Stichting NLnet (with European Commission backing\
 ; successor to the NGI Zero programme)\nLocation: Remote / worldwide. Indi
 viduals\, informal collectives\, nonprofits\, SMEs and universities from a
 ny country\; EU-backed funds want a European dimension\, and applicants ou
 tside Horizon Europe countries must explain the fit.\nAward: EUR 5\,000 to
  50\,000 for a first grant\, scalable in follow-ups\; the Restack fund alo
 ne will award EUR 7 million through 2030. No application fee.\nDuration: P
 roject-based\, typically up to about 12 months per plan\; calls recur roug
 hly every two months.\n\nMore: https://nlnet.nl/propose/?utm_source=artifi
 cialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://nlnet.nl/propose/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_med
 ium=referral
LOCATION:Remote / worldwide. Individuals\, informal collectives\, nonprofit
 s\, SMEs and universities from any country\; EU-backed funds want a Europe
 an dimension\, and applicants outside Horizon Europe countries must explai
 n the fit.
