UID:princeton-crockett-lab-postdoc-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261025T090229Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261120
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261121
SUMMARY:Deadline: Postdoctoral Fellow 2027\, Crockett Lab (Princeton Psycho
 logy and University Center for Human Values)
DESCRIPTION:Molly Crockett's lab at Princeton\, based in the Department of 
 Psychology and the University Center for Human Values\, is hiring a postdo
 c to start in summer or fall 2027. The research topic is flexible. The lab
  uses methods from computational social science and cognitive science info
 rmed by theory from science and technology studies and feminist epistemolo
 gy\, studying feedback loops between individual psychology\, institutions 
 and culture\, and how the tech industry co-opts these processes to concent
 rate power. It is especially interested in bridging quantitative and quali
 tative methods for understanding human experience\, and in how culture and
  power shape which questions are valued and which methods are legitimised.
  The lab is industry-independent and accepts no research funding from the 
 tech industry\; it uses a variety of ML methods and aims to develop though
 tful approaches to automation in scholarship\, so it suits researchers exc
 ited about AI in science but wary of hype and industry influence. WHAT YOU
  GET: an USD 80\,000 salary from stable institutional funds\, initial one-
 year appointment renewable up to three years. APPLICATION: via Interfolio\
 ; questions about fit to mj.crockett@princeton.edu. Review of applications
  begins 20 November 2026 and continues until the position is filled.\n\nOr
 ganisation: Princeton University\, Crockett Lab (Department of Psychology 
 and University Center for Human Values)\nLocation: Princeton\, New Jersey\
 , USA.\nAward: USD 80\,000 annual salary from a stable institutional fundi
 ng source (not a cancellable grant).\nDuration: Initial one-year appointme
 nt\, renewable up to three years\, starting summer or fall 2027.\n\nMore: 
 https://apply.interfolio.com/195297?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&
 utm_medium=referral
URL:https://apply.interfolio.com/195297?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantde
 sk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Princeton\, New Jersey\, USA.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:fas-metascience-fellowship-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261025T090229Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261109
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261110
SUMMARY:Deadline: FAS Metascience Fellowship 2027 (full-time placement in a
  US federal research agency)
DESCRIPTION:The Federation of American Scientists' Metascience Fellowship p
 laces three full-time fellows inside federal research agencies such as the
  NSF or DOE for one year\, after a pre-service residency at FAS. Fellows a
 dvise agency leaders on evidence-based research reform\, analyse grantmaki
 ng\, peer review and open-science practices\, design experiments with buil
 t-in evaluation\, write briefing memos\, coordinate metascience work acros
 s agencies and give hands-on technical help. Placements may be extended de
 pending on funding and performance. ELIGIBILITY: US citizens only\; curren
 t federal employees cannot apply. Mid- to senior-career professionals with
  an advanced degree or equivalent experience in a scientific\, engineering
  or public-policy field\, willing to work mostly in person in the Washingt
 on\, DC area. Fellows must start at FAS no later than 4 January 2027. Appl
 ications take a CV and three responses of up to 300 words each\, submitted
  through the FAS platform. DEADLINE: 9 November 2026\, 11:59PM ET\; late a
 pplications are not reviewed.\n\nOrganisation: Federation of American Scie
 ntists (FAS)\nLocation: Washington\, DC area\, United States. Full-time an
 d mostly in person at agency offices.\nAward: USD 174\,000 per year\, pror
 ated monthly\, plus USD 1\,500 for travel and USD 1\,500 for professional 
 development. Fellows are not eligible for employer-sponsored benefits\; th
 e salary is expected to cover health and living costs. No application fee.
 \nDuration: One year at a federal agency (extension possible)\, preceded b
 y a residency at FAS\; start no later than 4 January 2027.\n\nMore: https:
 //fas.org/career/metascience-fellowship/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrant
 desk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://fas.org/career/metascience-fellowship/?utm_source=artificialnou
 veaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Washington\, DC area\, United States. Full-time and mostly in pers
 on at agency offices.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:mozilla-incubator-human-scale-ai-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261025T090229Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261120
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261121
SUMMARY:Deadline: Mozilla Foundation Incubator: Human-Scale AI cohort 2027 
 (call for proposals)
DESCRIPTION:The Mozilla Foundation Incubator's next cohort funds seven Huma
 n-Scale AI projects: working AI technologies that are small (small models\
 , less compute\, able to run locally or on low-power devices)\, intentiona
 l (users and communities get insight into and control over their data\, an
 d systems can be configured\, forked or community-governed) and tailored (
 fit-for-purpose for a specific community\, context or problem\, with parti
 cular interest in resource-constrained regions\, people with disabilities 
 and other underserved groups). Projects must already be deployed with the 
 people they serve\, even at pilot scale\, and show early product-community
  fit. Not wanted: concepts without working technology\, standalone governa
 nce or policy work\, generic chatbots\, or products whose core depends on 
 a frontier model or a slimmed-down version of one. The cohort runs for 12 
 months from April 2027 with coaching\, a Mozilla programme officer\, netwo
 rk access and a showcase at the Mozilla Festival\; required sessions are a
 bout one or two hour-long virtual meetings a month\, and teams must work i
 n the open. ELIGIBILITY: worldwide\; you do not need to be a nonprofit but
  the project must have a charitable purpose and you must be legally able t
 o receive Mozilla Foundation grant funds. Applications in English (transla
 tion tools welcome). Multi-stage process: an initial project proposal\, th
 en a full application for a shortlist. Info session 12 November 2026\, 17:
 00 UTC. DEADLINE: Friday 20 November 2026\, 11:59PM PST (UTC-8).\n\nOrgani
 sation: Mozilla Foundation (Mozilla Foundation Incubator)\nLocation: Remot
 e cohort worldwide\, with a platform at the Mozilla Festival.\nAward: USD 
 300\,000 non-dilutive funding plus 12 months of support for each of seven 
 selected projects\; projects showing strong progress may receive up to USD
  200\,000 more and two further years of support\, for a total of up to USD
  500\,000 over three years. No application fee.\nDuration: 12 months from 
 April 2027\, with possible follow-on support for two more years.\n\nMore: 
 https://www.mozillafoundation.org/en/what-we-do/grantmaking/incubator/huma
 n-scale-ai/call-for-proposals/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_m
 edium=referral
URL:https://www.mozillafoundation.org/en/what-we-do/grantmaking/incubator/h
 uman-scale-ai/call-for-proposals/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&ut
 m_medium=referral
LOCATION:Remote cohort worldwide\, with a platform at the Mozilla Festival.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:foresight-ai-science-safety-nodes-rfp-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261025T090229Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261031
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261101
SUMMARY:Deadline: Foresight Institute: AI for Science and Safety Nodes RFP 
 2026 (Local Compute\; Coordination and Accountability\; AI-first Science)
DESCRIPTION:Foresight Institute's AI for Science and Safety Nodes request f
 or proposals funds open\, AI-first projects across three calls: I. Local C
 ompute (compute that individuals and communities physically own and contro
 l)\, II. Coordination and Accountability (supercollaboration and decentral
 ised alignment\, human empowerment\, and AI insurance and open governance:
  multi-agent oversight and verification\, tools for collective deliberatio
 n\, decision rules for when human control adds value\, and independent ris
 k assessment or insurance mechanisms for frontier labs)\, and III. AI-firs
 t Science (automated nanotechnology\, whole-brain emulation\, frontier bio
 ). Grantees can also get workspace in the San Francisco or Berlin AI Nodes
  (a community xNode runs in Cape Town) and private compute. All funded cod
 e\, data and outputs must be open-sourced. Projects are judged on fit with
  the focus area\, impact on reducing existential risk from AI\, feasibilit
 y within 1 to 3 years\, AI-first working methods\, ability to execute\, an
 d high-risk\, high-reward potential. ELIGIBILITY: individuals\, teams and 
 organisations worldwide\; nonprofits and for-profits welcome (for-profits 
 must justify the need for grant funding). Priority goes to applicants who 
 want to work in person at one of the Nodes\, but it is not required. Revie
 w takes about three months\; applications can opt in to sharing with Light
 cone Commons. DEADLINE: 31 October 2026\, 23:59 PDT.\n\nOrganisation: Fore
 sight Institute\nLocation: Remote-friendly worldwide\; optional in-person 
 membership at the Foresight AI Nodes in San Francisco or Berlin.\nAward: G
 rants typically USD 30\,000 to 100\,000 (smaller awards for the Human Empo
 werment and AI Insurance and Open Governance areas\, larger for the rest\;
  bigger amounts possible for the right project)\, usually paid as one lump
  sum\, with up to 10 percent overhead. Optional office space in San Franci
 sco or Berlin and access to private compute clusters. No application fee.\
 nDuration: Short-term and multi-year projects\; larger multi-year grants a
 re paid in milestone tranches.\n\nMore: https://foresight.org/grants/ai-sc
 ience-safety-nodes-rfp/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=r
 eferral
URL:https://foresight.org/grants/ai-science-safety-nodes-rfp/?utm_source=ar
 tificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Remote-friendly worldwide\; optional in-person membership at the F
 oresight AI Nodes in San Francisco or Berlin.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:rji-professional-innovation-fellowships-2027@artificialnouveau.github.i
 o
DTSTAMP:20261025T090229Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270108
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270109
SUMMARY:Deadline: RJI Professional Innovation Fellowships 2027 (Individual\
 , Institutional and Emerging Technology tracks)
DESCRIPTION:The Reynolds Journalism Institute at the University of Missouri
  funds people and teams to build and launch a tool\, workflow or product t
 hat helps newsrooms\, in three tracks: Individual (USD 75\,000)\, Institut
 ional (USD 75\,000\, paid to a host organisation or the fellow) and Emergi
 ng Technology (USD 100\,000\, where AI or another new technology must be e
 ssential to the solution). The output must be a free\, open-source resourc
 e usable by US journalists\; tools limited to one city or state are unlike
 ly to be funded. The fellowship is remote and runs for eight months from 2
 8 June 2027 with an in-person kickoff at RJI and a couple of paid visits. 
 ELIGIBILITY: anyone\, anywhere\; no age\, background or journalism credent
 ial required. Applications open 2 November 2026 on Submittable\; a shortli
 st is invited in early to mid February 2027 to submit a fuller application
 \, with finalist interviews 5 to 23 April 2027. DEADLINE: 8 January 2027 (
 first round\; no time zone stated\, RJI is on US Central time).\n\nOrganis
 ation: Reynolds Journalism Institute (University of Missouri)\nLocation: R
 emote\, with a few paid visits to the Reynolds Journalism Institute in Col
 umbia\, Missouri\, United States.\nAward: USD 75\,000 for the Individual a
 nd Institutional tracks\, USD 100\,000 for the Emerging Technology track\,
  paid in three instalments tied to deliverables\; RJI also pays for the fe
 llow's visits to its Columbia\, Missouri campus. No application fee.\nDura
 tion: Eight months from 28 June 2027.\n\nMore: https://rjionline.org/about
 -rji-fellowships/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referra
 l
URL:https://rjionline.org/about-rji-fellowships/?utm_source=artificialnouve
 augrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Remote\, with a few paid visits to the Reynolds Journalism Institu
 te in Columbia\, Missouri\, United States.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:schaufler-residency-tu-dresden-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261025T090229Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261109
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261110
SUMMARY:Deadline: Schaufler Residency@TU Dresden 2027 (six-month art and sc
 ience residency\, Energy Cultures in Transition)
DESCRIPTION:The Schaufler Lab at TUD Dresden University of Technology\, a j
 oint project with The Schaufler Foundation\, invites applications for its 
 six-month artist-in-residence at the interface of art and science for 2027
 . The theme of the Lab's third funding phase (2027 to 2030) is Energy Cult
 ures in Transition: how forms of energy and energy transitions shape and a
 re shaped by cultural practices\, value systems\, power relations\, enviro
 nmental relationships and imaginaries of the future. Residents work with t
 he researchers of the Schaufler Kolleg graduate college and the wider univ
 ersity\, with access to humanities\, natural-science and engineering labs\
 , and give lectures\, talks and workshops\, including a collaboration with
  the Dresden University of Fine Arts. Past residents include Quadrature\, 
 Mario Pfeifer\, Rosa Barba and Esmeralda Conde Ruiz. ELIGIBILITY: internat
 ionally active artists or artist groups in media art\, conceptual art\, pe
 rformance and related fields with completed international projects and exh
 ibitions\, an interest in exchange between artistic and scientific researc
 h\, and proficient German or English\; presence on site in Dresden is requ
 ired by arrangement. Apply with a form\, CV\, portfolio\, project proposal
  (up to 10\,000 characters)\, project plan with potential TUD collaborator
 s\, a three-minute video and a recent letter of recommendation\, as one PD
 F by email. The call is subject to final funding approval. Residency start
 s April 2027. DEADLINE: 9 November 2026.\n\nOrganisation: Schaufler Lab@TU
  Dresden (TUD Dresden University of Technology and The Schaufler Foundatio
 n)\nLocation: Dresden\, Germany. Studio on the TU Dresden campus\; on-site
  presence by arrangement.\nAward: Fellowship of EUR 3\,000 net per month f
 or six months (EUR 18\,000)\, plus a production grant of up to EUR 10\,000
  for a solo exhibition at the TUD University Gallery in autumn 2027\, a st
 udio on campus and help finding accommodation. No application fee.\nDurati
 on: Six months from April 2027.\n\nMore: https://tu-dresden.de/gsw/schaufl
 erlab/schaufler-residency?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium
 =referral
URL:https://tu-dresden.de/gsw/schauflerlab/schaufler-residency?utm_source=a
 rtificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Dresden\, Germany. Studio on the TU Dresden campus\; on-site prese
 nce by arrangement.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:traces-art-science-energypolis-residency-2027@artificialnouveau.github.
 io
DTSTAMP:20261025T090229Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261122
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261123
SUMMARY:Deadline: TRACES Art & Science @ Energypolis 2027: residency at the
  EPFL Laboratory for Energy Materials (Sion)
DESCRIPTION:TRACES is a new art and science residency run by the Foundation
  for the Sustainable Development of Mountain Regions (FDDM) with EPFL Vala
 is-Wallis\, Energypolis\, the City of Sion and the Canton of Valais. The 2
 027 pilot embeds one visual artist for three months in Prof. Sascha Feldma
 nn's Laboratory for Energy Materials at EPFL\, which works on light-matter
  interactions and soft semiconductors for flexible solar cells\, energy-ef
 ficient screens and emerging quantum technologies. The artist develops ori
 ginal work in dialogue with the lab around the energy transition and the m
 aterials of the future\, with studio and production space\, scientific men
 toring and a public final presentation on 15 April 2027. ELIGIBILITY: conf
 irmed\, professional international visual artists aged 25 or over who fini
 shed their studies at least two years ago and have at least two years of p
 rofessional practice\; applications in English or French with a letter of 
 intent (two A4 pages)\, portfolio and CV via the online form. Laureate sel
 ected 7 December 2026. DEADLINE: 22 November 2026\, 23:59 Swiss time (CET)
 .\n\nOrganisation: Foundation for the Sustainable Development of Mountain 
 Regions (FDDM) with EPFL Valais-Wallis\nLocation: Energypolis campus\, Sio
 n\, Valais\, Switzerland. In person.\nAward: Artist stipend of CHF 2\,000 
 per month (CHF 6\,000 total) covering living and research costs\, housing 
 in Sion\, travel from home and back up to CHF 1\,500\, and a separate prod
 uction budget set by the curator. No application fee.\nDuration: Three mon
 ths\, 11 January to 18 April 2027.\n\nMore: https://www.traces-opencall.ch
 /en?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.traces-opencall.ch/en?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk
 &utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Energypolis campus\, Sion\, Valais\, Switzerland. In person.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:art4mental-open-call-vr-artists-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261025T090229Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261111
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261112
SUMMARY:Deadline: ART4MENTAL open call for artists: VR content for mental-h
 ealth support (EUR 5\,000 sub-grants)
DESCRIPTION:ART4MENTAL is a Creative Europe project (partners in Ukraine\, 
 Poland\, Czechia\, Estonia\, Sweden and Austria) selecting 20 artists to c
 reate immersive VR content and scenarios used in art-therapy and mental-he
 alth support sessions across Ukraine and the EU. Selected artists get prof
 essional training in VR technology and trauma-informed design\, local boot
 camps\, a residency in Ukraine's Carpathian Mountains\, study visits to re
 habilitation centres\, ongoing collaboration with mental-health profession
 als\, and present their work at European exhibitions and conferences\, inc
 luding an international exhibition in Poland. ELIGIBILITY: the official pa
 ge says residents of EU countries and Ukraine with a proven artistic pract
 ice and full availability for all mandatory activities\; the On the Move l
 isting adds that at least 10 of the 20 places go to artists from Ukraine a
 nd at least one each to Czechia\, Estonia\, Sweden and Austria\, so applic
 ants from other EU countries are eligible but not prioritised. Two stages:
  online form with supporting documents\, then an online interview\; select
 ed artists announced January 2027. DEADLINE: 11 November 2026 per On the M
 ove (the official page only says November 2026\; no time zone stated).\n\n
 Organisation: ART4MENTAL (Creative Europe project)\nLocation: Hybrid: onli
 ne training plus a residency in the Carpathian Mountains\, Ukraine\, and a
 n exhibition in Poland.\nAward: Sub-grant of up to EUR 5\,000 per artist f
 or 20 selected artists (EUR 100\,000 pool)\, plus VR training\, mentorship
 \, a residency in the Ukrainian Carpathians and exhibition opportunities. 
 No application fee.\nDuration: Selection by January 2027\; residency and e
 xhibition dates not yet published.\n\nMore: https://www.art4mental.com/app
 lication?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.art4mental.com/application?utm_source=artificialnouveaugran
 tdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Hybrid: online training plus a residency in the Carpathian Mountai
 ns\, Ukraine\, and an exhibition in Poland.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:alpaca-festival-2027-open-call@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261025T090229Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261101
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261102
SUMMARY:Deadline: Alpaca Festival 2027: Open Call for Pattern-Based Perform
 ances\, Workshops and Talks (Sheffield\, UK)
DESCRIPTION:Alpaca is a festival and conference on algorithmic patterns in 
 the creative arts\, run by the non-profit Pattern Club in Sheffield. It br
 ings together live coders\, weavers\, braiders\, origami makers\, musician
 s and other practitioners who make patterns by procedure\, and it welcomes
  contemporary algorithmic art that is human-authored. THEME (talks): makin
 g languages and notations for making patterns\, with unexpected interpreta
 tions welcome. WHAT YOU CAN PROPOSE: live performances\, hands-on workshop
 s\, and roughly 20-minute conference talks\; accepted abstracts (max two p
 ages) are published open access with a DOI and may be invited into an edit
 ed volume. WHAT YOU GET: performers receive an artist fee plus national tr
 avel\; workshop leaders receive an artist fee\, materials and national tra
 vel. The organisers state they cannot confirm fee amounts at this stage an
 d may cover extra costs on request\; international travel is not covered a
 part from a small European train budget. Talks are unpaid: in-person speak
 ers get a free festival pass and lunch on the conference days. EXCLUSIONS:
  submissions focused on generative AI or unsupervised pattern generation b
 y LLMs. APPLICATION: via the online form at calls.alpaca.cc\; questions to
  contact@alpaca.cc. DEADLINE: 1 November 2026.\n\nOrganisation: Pattern Cl
 ub (Alpaca Festival)\nLocation: Sheffield\, UK\, with some talks and activ
 ities online. Open internationally\, but only national (UK) travel is cove
 red\, plus a small budget for European train travel.\nAward: Performances:
  artist fee plus national travel expenses. Workshops: artist fee\, materia
 ls expenses and national travel expenses. Fee amounts are not yet confirme
 d (tight budget)\; additional costs may be covered on request. Internation
 al travel is not covered beyond a small European train budget. Conference 
 talks: no fee or expenses\, in-person speakers get a free festival weekend
  pass and lunch on 6 and 7 May. No application fee.\nDuration: Festival 6 
 to 9 May 2027: conference talks 6 and 7 May\, workshops and performances 7
  to 9 May. Decisions expected December 2026.\n\nMore: https://alpaca.cc/ca
 ll/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://alpaca.cc/call/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_mediu
 m=referral
LOCATION:Sheffield\, UK\, with some talks and activities online. Open inter
 nationally\, but only national (UK) travel is covered\, plus a small budge
 t for European train travel.
END:VEVENT
