SUMMARY:Deadline: Creative Europe MEDIA: European Slate Development 2027 (E
 UR 90\,000 to 510\,000 per slate\, incl. immersive)
DESCRIPTION:The MEDIA Slate Development call (CREA-MEDIA-2027-DEVSLATE) fun
 ds established European independent production companies to develop a slat
 e of audiovisual works with cross-border potential: fiction\, animation\, 
 creative documentary and immersive projects. WHO: a single applicant only\
 , an independent European production company with a recent international t
 rack record\; a company can coordinate only one of Slate Development\, Co-
 Development\, mini-slate or Video Games and Immersive Content Development 
 in the same year. WHAT YOU GET: a slate grant of EUR 90\,000 to EUR 510\,0
 00\, built from fixed lump sums per project type\, from a total budget of 
 EUR 22\,374\,320. APPLICATION: via the EU Funding and Tenders portal. DEAD
 LINE: 1 December 2026\, 17:00 CET (Brussels).\n\nOrganisation: Creative Eu
 rope MEDIA (European Commission / EACEA)\nLocation: EU Member States\, EEA
  and countries associated to Creative Europe MEDIA. For organisations (leg
 al entities) established in a MEDIA country\; natural persons cannot apply
 . Single established independent production company.\nAward: EUR 90\,000 t
 o EUR 510\,000 per slate\, built from fixed lump sums per project type (fo
 r example EUR 30\,000 for a one-off creative documentary\, EUR 60\,000 for
  an animated series\, EUR 75\,000 for a fiction series budgeted EUR 5-20 m
 illion). Total call budget EUR 22\,374\,320. No application fee.\nDuration
 : Projects normally up to 36 months. Call opened 30 September 2026.\n\nMor
 e: https://ec.europa.eu/info/funding-tenders/opportunities/portal/screen/o
 pportunities/topic-details/CREA-MEDIA-2027-DEVSLATE?utm_source=artificialn
 ouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://ec.europa.eu/info/funding-tenders/opportunities/portal/screen/o
 pportunities/topic-details/CREA-MEDIA-2027-DEVSLATE?utm_source=artificialn
 ouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
