SUMMARY:Deadline: Creative Europe MEDIA: European Co-Development 2027 (up t
 o EUR 120\,000 plus EUR 60\,000 per extra partner\, film\, series and imme
 rsive)
DESCRIPTION:The MEDIA Co-Development call (CREA-MEDIA-2027-CODEV) supports 
 European independent production companies developing a work together: feat
 ure films\, shorts\, series\, creative documentaries and narrative VR or i
 mmersive projects intended for cross-border audiences. WHO: consortia of a
 t least two independent European production companies from two MEDIA count
 ries\; the coordinator needs a recent international production track recor
 d (since 2020). A company can coordinate only one of CODEV\, Slate Develop
 ment\, mini-slate or Video Games and Immersive Content Development in the 
 same year. WHAT YOU GET: a lump-sum grant at a 70 percent funding rate of 
 up to EUR 120\,000 for two partners plus EUR 60\,000 per extra partner\, o
 r up to EUR 200\,000 plus EUR 100\,000 per extra partner for drama series 
 budgeted at EUR 20 million or more\; total budget EUR 12\,500\,000. APPLIC
 ATION: via the EU Funding and Tenders portal. DEADLINE: 2 March 2027\, 17:
 00 CET (Brussels).\n\nOrganisation: Creative Europe MEDIA (European Commis
 sion / EACEA)\nLocation: EU Member States\, EEA and countries associated t
 o Creative Europe MEDIA. For organisations (legal entities) established in
  a MEDIA country\; natural persons cannot apply. Consortia of at least two
  independent production companies from two MEDIA countries.\nAward: Lump s
 um at a 70 percent funding rate: up to EUR 120\,000 for a two-partner cons
 ortium plus EUR 60\,000 per additional partner\; high-budget drama series 
 (EUR 20 million or more) up to EUR 200\,000 plus EUR 100\,000 per addition
 al partner. Total call budget EUR 12\,500\,000. No application fee.\nDurat
 ion: Projects normally up to 30 months. Call opened 30 September 2026.\n\n
 More: https://ec.europa.eu/info/funding-tenders/opportunities/portal/scree
 n/opportunities/topic-details/CREA-MEDIA-2027-CODEV?utm_source=artificialn
