 ds innovative tools\, models and solutions applicable across the audiovisu
 al and other cultural and creative sectors. Every project must involve the
  audiovisual sector (video games included) plus at least one of music\, bo
 oks or museums. The 2027 call is explicitly aligned with the EU Apply AI S
 trategy\, including AI for content discoverability\, and covers virtual wo
 rlds\, AI-\, data- and blockchain-based business tools (rights management\
 , monetisation\, data analytics) and greener practices. WHO: a single orga
 nisation or a consortium of two or more\, established in a Creative Europe
  country\; individuals cannot apply. WHAT YOU GET: an actual-cost grant at
  an 80 percent funding rate from a total budget of EUR 7\,183\,502\, with 
 financial support to third parties of up to EUR 60\,000 each allowed. APPL
 ICATION: via the EU Funding and Tenders portal. DEADLINE: 22 April 2027\, 
 17:00 CET (Brussels).\n\nOrganisation: Creative Europe Cross-sectoral stra
 nd (European Commission / EACEA)\nLocation: EU Member States and countries
  associated to Creative Europe. For organisations (legal entities) establi
 shed in an eligible country\; natural persons cannot apply.\nAward: Total 
 call budget EUR 7\,183\,502\; no fixed cap per project\; actual-cost grant
  at an 80 percent funding rate. Projects may re-grant up to EUR 60\,000 pe
 r third party. No application fee.\nDuration: Projects normally up to 24 m
 onths. Call opened 22 October 2026.\n\nMore: https://ec.europa.eu/info/fun
 ding-tenders/opportunities/portal/screen/opportunities/topic-details/CREA-
 CROSS-2027-INNOVLAB?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=refer
 ral
